{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game part game part","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md","fileName":"Game Part.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Part","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Systems]] [[Game Mechanics and Rules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Systems","Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Attribute","Game Verb","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game part game part","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md","fileName":"Game Part.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Part","heading":"Game Part","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A game part is a physical, conceptual, or representational element with internal state and behaviors. At the atomic level it is specified through [[Game Attribute|attributes]], values, and functions rather than through smaller systemic loops.\n\nParts are the nouns and verbs from which loops arise: attributes hold state, while behaviors change resources and connect parts. Each included part should support player interaction, a system purpose, or the internal model needed for the experience.\n\nFrom the player's perspective, a part can function as the object of a [[Game Verb]]: the thing acted on that completes an interactive relationship. Useful objects reinforce important verbs and interact with other objects instead of existing for one isolated case.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Systems","Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Attribute","Game Verb","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game part game part","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Part.md","fileName":"Game Part.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Part","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Systems","Game Mechanics and Rules","Game Attribute","Game Verb","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}